    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW26B4bFUyCp9qHtNggCR8C2U)_\n\n## Summary\n\n- New `M-x sp-author-notes-bibtex-author`: runs the BibTeX search for the author note in the current buffer only. `sp-author-notes-bibtex` (all authors) is unchanged.\n- Name forms are the note title plus its `ROAM_ALIASES`. When `sp-bibprocess` is loaded, names with the same surname and compatible given names (the lint matcher from #354) count as possible matches.\n- Report is a `sp-batch-report`: no litnote (exact), no litnote (possible), litnote exists but is not linked to the note, then already in the note. `d`/`u` drop and restore, `g` re-reads.\n- `A` adds the exact items after one question: new litnote (`citar-create-note`) or the `pub-author`/`pub-editor` line in an existing litnote; then the note gets its Works / Edited works headings and tables as in `sp-author-notes-works-convert`. Possible matches only with `sp-author-notes-bibtex-apply-possible`.\n- Literate doc: new \"One author\" section in `sp-org-lint.org` (bullet list); `.el` tangled from it.\n\n## Testing\n\n- 5 new ERT tests in `sp-author-notes-bibtex-test.el`; all 13 tests there plus `sp-async-work` and `sp-batch-report` pass on Emacs 29.3.\n- Not run on the real vault, and the Works table fill needs vulpea (not available in the test run).\n- No CHANGELOG edits.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9EoHmHrUjd52v9LXg)_",
